## ARCHITECTURE REFERENCE

### F.R.E.S.H. Pillar Structure
Each pillar should function independently but share a common user context:

```
/food      → Nutrition tracking, USDA search, meal templates, food log, daily/weekly summaries
/rest      → Stress management, meditation, sleep tracking, restoration content
/exercise  → Workout library, activity tracking, exercise demo videos
/spirit    → Faith deepening, journaling, spiritual Q&A, daily scripture
/habits    → Consistency tracking, streak badges, gamification, daily check-ins
```

### Database Conventions (Supabase)
- All user-facing tables MUST have RLS policies filtering on `auth.uid()`
- Profile table: `id`, `user_id` (FK to auth.users), `gender`, `age`, `preferred_units`, `height_cm`, `weight_kg`, `goal`, `activity_level`, `onboarding_complete` (boolean), `created_at`, `updated_at`
- Food log table: entries tied to `user_id` with timestamp, meal data, and calculated per-serving nutrition
- When querying profiles: ALWAYS handle three states: (1) profile found and complete, (2) profile found but incomplete, (3) query failed/returned empty due to auth or RLS issues. State 3 is NOT the same as "new user."

### Meal Template Data Structure
Every meal template entry must include:
```
{
  name: string,               // "Chicken & Whole Wheat Pasta Primavera"
  category: string,           // "dinner" | "lunch" | "breakfast" | "snack"
  servings: number,           // e.g. 4
  portion_label: string,      // "Female portion"
  ingredients: [
    {
      name: string,           // "Whole wheat pasta (cooked)"
      amount: number,         // 600
      unit: string,           // "g"
      calories: number,       // 942 (NOT dry weight calories)
      weight_state: string    // "cooked" | "dry" | "raw" — REQUIRED for grains/pasta
    }
  ],
  total_calories: number,     // Sum of all ingredient calories
  per_serving_calories: number // total_calories / servings — THIS IS WHAT GETS DISPLAYED
}
```

### API Integration
- **USDA Food API** for food search and nutrition data (replaced FatSecret)
- All API keys stored in Vercel environment variables, never in client code
- API calls should include error handling with user-friendly fallback messages

