## SIGNALS — ADAPTIVE BEHAVIOUR RULES

| Signal | Response |
|--------|----------|
| Owner reports a calorie value is wrong | Audit ALL meal templates for the same pattern (total not divided by servings), not just the one reported |
| Owner reports a feature "keeps breaking" | Search git history for previous fixes to the same feature. Identify why the fix didn't persist — was it overwritten by a later change? Was the root cause not addressed? |
| Owner provides a PDF with recipe data | Extract FEMALE portion sizes only unless told otherwise. Target calorie ranges: breakfast ~250-350, lunch ~300-400, dinner ~600-800 |
| Owner says "this was already fixed" | This means a regression. Check git blame on the relevant files. Find what change reintroduced the bug. Fix it AND add a guard to prevent recurrence. |
| A Supabase query returns empty unexpectedly | NEVER treat this as "no data exists." First check: is the user authenticated? Is the RLS policy allowing the read? Is the query filtering on the correct user_id? Only after confirming all three should you treat it as genuinely empty. |
| Build fails on Vercel | Check for hydration mismatches first (most common), then missing environment variables, then dependency issues |
| Mobile layout looks wrong | Check the sidebar collapse, video embed responsive wrappers, and parent container overflow properties — these are the three most common mobile layout failures in this project |

